DAY 2 – Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)
Very important for Spring Framework
2.1 What is OOP?
Definition: Object-Oriented Programming is a programming approach in which we organize code using classes and objects.

Instead of writing all the code inside one large method, we divide our application into smaller, reusable components.
Real-world example: College Management System
Think about a college.

It contains:
- Students
- Teachers
- Courses
- Departments
- Classrooms
Each entity has properties and behaviours.

For example:
Entity	Properties	Behaviours
Student	Name, ID, marks	Study, attend
Teacher	Name, subject	Teach, evaluate
Course	Name, duration	Enroll, complete
Account	Balance, number	Deposit, withdraw
